description: "For the best chicken Parmesan, try Chef John's version that's pan-fried and then baked, delivering impressive results with a crispier crust than most recipes."
---

> Time: PT45M

= Ingredients

@skinless, boneless chicken breast halves{5}\
@salt and freshly ground black pepper to taste{}\
@large eggs{2 1/2}\
@panko bread crumbs, or more as needed{1 1/4%cup}\
@grated Parmesan cheese, divided{15/16%cup}\
@all-purpose flour, or more if needed{2 1/2%tablespoons}\
@olive oil for frying, or as needed{5/8%cup}\
@prepared tomato sauce{5/8%cup}\
@fresh mozzarella, cut into small cubes{5/16%cup}\
@chopped fresh basil{5/16%cup}\
@grated provolone cheese{5/8%cup}\
@olive oil{2 1/2%teaspoons}

= Directions
Gather the ingredients. Preheat the oven to 450 degrees F (230 degrees C).

Place chicken breasts between two sheets of heavy plastic (resealable freezer bags work well) on a solid, level surface. Firmly pound chicken with the smooth side of a meat mallet to a thickness of 1/2-inch.

Season chicken thoroughly with salt and pepper. Using a sifter or strainer, sprinkle flour over chicken breasts, evenly coating both sides.

Beat eggs in a shallow bowl and set aside. Mix bread crumbs with most of the Parmesan cheese in a separate bowl, reserving the rest for topping. Dip a flour-coated chicken breast in beaten eggs. Transfer breast to the bread crumb mixture, pressing crumbs into both sides. Repeat for each breast. Let chicken rest for 10 to 15 minutes.

Heat the frying oil in a large skillet over medium-high heat until it begins to shimmer. Cook chicken in batches, so you do not overcrowd the pan, until golden, about 2 minutes per side. The chicken will finish cooking in the oven.

Transfer chicken to a baking dish. Divide the tomato sauce, mozzarella cheese, fresh basil, and provolone cheese evenly over the chicken. Sprinkle the reserved Parmesan over top and drizzle with the remaining olive oil.

Bake in the preheated oven until cheese is browned and bubbly and chicken breasts are no longer pink in the center, 15 to 20 minutes. An instant-read thermometer inserted into the center should read at least 165 degrees F (74 degrees C). Let chicken rest briefly before serving.
